  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 105 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nQuiet and benign weather will persist through the remainder of the\nwork week. A shortwave trough grazing northern and eastern New\nMexico overnight into Thursday will drop temperatures a couple of\ndegrees for Thursday and Friday. Highs will run about 3 to 6\ndegrees below seasonal normals. With lighter winds Thursday night,\novernight lows could drop into the upper-30s over the usual cold\nspots in the lowland deserts, especially in the Tularosa and\nJornada basins. No new freeze areas are expected.\n\nA deep trough and weak southeasterly push or backdoor cold front\nwill bring increasing chances for light rain showers Friday night\ninto Saturday. There remains uncertainty with how far south the \ntrough will track, or if it will close off into a low aloft. A\nclosed low scenario would favor at least some isolated\nthunderstorms. Higher terrain areas, and lowlands east of El Paso\nlook to have the best shot at measurable rainfall.",
